te inferior, lo esperable serían 14,8 contratos. La razón entre observados y esperados es 6,2, con un intervalo de confianza del 95 % de 4,5 a 8,6. En diciembre se adjudicó el 8 % de los contratos junto al límite, mientras que diciembre supone el 8 % de todos sus contratos de servicios y suministros. Los contratos junto al límite se reparten entre 79 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.800 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: La concentración de contratos al límite no indica malas prácticas. Puede ser debido a necesidades específicas o a precios de mercado. No implica que se hayan sobrepasado los límites ni que se hayan actuado de forma irregular.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1] y [2] atienden necesidades similares. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas distintas. Analizar si los contratos al límite coinciden con otros en el mismo periodo.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 92 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 14.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 6.2, with a 95% confidence interval of 4.5 to 8.6. December accounts for 8% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 8% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 3. Contract [1], for 14,800 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not indicate improper conduct. It could reflect market pricing, budget constraints, or separate needs. Statistical patterns alone do not prove wrongdoing in procurement processes.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to confirm the service type and whether it aligns with the body's needs. Review awardee A's other contracts to see if they repeat the same service or vendor. Look for patterns in December awards to determine if seasonal factors influenced the contract distribution.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["E3gH3nqeRqfXOjazN1Dw9Q%3D%3D","mGyyhJC5%2FI87%2B9FIQYNjeQ%3D%3D","1ReSQVnXrmr%2Fa9DgO%2BoYKQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}